Assignment 1. JavaScript Calculator using Functions 
• Aim: To design and implement a basic arithmetic calculator using JavaScript 
functions and conditional logic. 
• Learning Objectives: Understand JavaScript variables, basic operators, function 
definitions, parameters, and control flow structures (switch or if-else). 
• Theoretical Background: JavaScript functions as reusable blocks of code; using 
conditional statements to route execution based on user input (e.g., operator 
selection). 
• Detailed Requirements: 
o Implement separate helper functions for add(a, b), subtract(a, b), 
multiply(a, b), and divide(a, b). 
o Implement a driver function or prompt-based interface that takes two 
numbers and an operator (+, −, ∗, /) as input. 
o Handle edge cases such as division by zero with an appropriate warning. 
• Execution Step: Run the script using a browser console, or by embedding it in an 
HTML file and opening it in a web browser. 
